<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Auto Backup rules for Android 10 – 11 (`android:fullBackupContent`). API 31+ reads
  data_extraction_rules.xml instead; both exist because minSdk is 26 and the two formats are not
  interchangeable.

  What is kept is everything the user chose, and it all lives under `files/`: the settings DataStore
  (`files/datastore/nordprice_settings.preferences_pb`, which `AppSettings.persist` writes) and the
  day cache (`files/price_cache`). What is dropped is the whole `shared_prefs` domain, which holds
  no user-visible state but does hold credentials: the Firebase Auth anonymous account and its
  refresh token, the FCM registration token, UMP's consent record, and `nordprice_notifications.xml`
  with the installation UUID. That is the platform's own advice for this exact case: device-specific
  identifiers, and an FCM registration token in particular, must not be restored onto a second
  install. Restoring them would make two phones the *same* device to the backend, because the device
  row is keyed by the Auth uid, and the newer phone would quietly take over the older one's alerts.

  Dropping the locale AppCompat stores for Android 12 and below costs nothing: the language is also
  in the DataStore, and `AppShell` pushes it back into `AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales` on
  the next launch.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude
        domain="sharedpref"
        path="." />
</full-backup-content>
